  "ranking_metric": "median_minutes_to_measured_starred_restaurants",
  "ranking_metric_explained": "Each hotel's rank is the median modelled door-to-door time to the starred restaurants that could be measured for it. A lower median is better. The metric is chosen because the requested 'count within 1 hour' turned out not to discriminate: every hotel reaches every measured starred restaurant inside 60 minutes, so the count is identical and the tie has to be broken by something that is actually measured.",
  "why_the_1h_count_is_not_a_ranking": "starred_restaurants_within_60_min_total is published for every hotel and is the same number for all of them. That is a real result of the measurement, not a placeholder: Midtown and the Financial District are both within an hour of every measured starred restaurant on the timetable used.",
  "sample_used_for_the_rank": "wednesday 12:00 local departure",
  "sensitivity_note": "median_spread_between_windows_min shows how much the median moves across the four samples (weekday/Saturday \u00d7 12:00/18:00). A rank whose spread overlaps the next hotel's median is a tie, not a win.",
